      "nets": ["GND", "Display_Power_Switch"],
      "observed": "C1 is populated as 0.1uF/16V between Display_Power_Switch and GND.",
      "expected": "The specification's EPD-driver BOM match requires C1 to be 1uF/25V, as part of the PDI C2 default group used by C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"C1\")\n      (value \"0.1uF/16V\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "C2 default: 1 µF/25 V | C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 µF/25 V"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "C1 0 Display_Power_Switch 0.1u"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The EPD boost input/power-switch rail has less bulk decoupling than intended and a lower voltage rating, which can increase ripple/noise and may destabilize the EPD charge-pump/boost converter.",
      "confidence": 0.75
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files otherwise follow the specification closely, but C1 on the EPD power rail is 0.1uF/16V instead of the specified 1uF/25V, indicating a component-value anomaly."
}

